    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_741d56ba",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a close-up of chef Gordon Ramsay with an angry expression, overlaid with the text 'if they steal this one i'm buying a horse.' The scene is a meme format that uses Ramsay's well-known fiery temper and dramatic reactions to convey exaggerated frustration or disbelief. The text is a hyperbolic, humorous statement implying that if someone takes something valuable (implied to be Ramsay himself or his reputation), the speaker will make a ridiculous, disproportionate response — buying a horse — to signal extreme annoyance. While the meme is intended as comedic and satirical, its harmfulness stems from the potential to be misinterpreted or used to mock individuals or groups in a way that could be seen as threatening or abusive, especially if applied to real people or situations. The meme does not contain explicit hate speech or targeted discrimination against protected groups, but its exaggerated, confrontational tone can be perceived as aggressive or potentially harmful in sensitive contexts. The overall intent is to elicit laughter through absurdity and the juxtaposition of Ramsay's intense persona with an illogical, over-the-top consequence.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8a542d15"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
