      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b9de42cc",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "The text 'if they steal this one' maps to Gordon Ramsay as the entity being referred to.",
      "description": "The phrase 'if they steal this one' is a hyperbolic statement implying that if someone takes Gordon Ramsay (or his reputation, status, or something he represents), the speaker will react with extreme frustration. The visual material of Gordon Ramsay, with his angry expression and confrontational posture, is mapped onto the textual entity 'this one' to signify that he is the object of the hypothetical theft. This mapping relies on the visual representation of Ramsay's persona as a valuable, irreplaceable, or highly prized entity in the context of celebrity culture and his public image.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8a542d15"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9b5b1e4f",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual entity 'this one' referring to Gordon Ramsay",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'if they steal this one', where 'this one' is semiotically mapped onto Gordon Ramsay (VisualMaterial entity). The user imagines themselves as the speaker of the text, projecting their own perspective onto the meme's scenario. The projection is onto the textual material because the text explicitly frames the hypothetical theft as targeting 'this one', which the user interprets as referring to Ramsay. The user is not directly projected onto the scene or the visual material of Ramsay as a separate entity, but rather onto the textual statement that uses Ramsay as its referent. This projection is implicit, relying on the user's understanding of the meme format and Ramsay's persona.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8a542d15"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c601cda3",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme uses hyperbolic and confrontational humor to exaggerate frustration, which can be perceived as aggressive or potentially harmful in sensitive contexts. The phrase 'I'm buying a horse' as a disproportionate response to theft implies extreme annoyance and could be misinterpreted as threatening or abusive if applied to real people or situations.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8a542d15"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
